{"uid":"progs/piano/piano.c::MAX_AUDIO_MS","name":"MAX_AUDIO_MS","qualname":"MAX_AUDIO_MS","kind":"macro","file":"progs/piano/piano.c","line":76,"end_line":76,"language":"c","signature":"#define MAX_AUDIO_MS","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Upper bound on audio rendered per frame, in milliseconds.","description":"The kernel-side audio ring absorbs up to ~3 seconds of buffered PCM, so a slow frame can render more without starving the speaker.  The clamp is kept conservative to avoid unbounded per-frame work.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/piano/piano.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"progs/piano/piano.c::PIANO_FRAME_MS","name":"PIANO_FRAME_MS","qualname":"PIANO_FRAME_MS","kind":"macro","file":"progs/piano/piano.c","line":84,"end_line":95,"language":"c","signature":"#define PIANO_FRAME_MS","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Per-frame render bite: after a stall the backlog is paced over several frames instead of one giant catch-up render, bounding the worst-case CPU spike while the debt below is preserved, so not a single millisecond of audio is lost.","description":"Must cover a typical frame time (nk rasterize 800x360 + nk_frame composite costs 30-50 ms in QEMU): a 15 ms bite renders at 15/40 = 0.37x wall-clock and sounds slow/low even with a trivial synth, which is why the bite stays just under one DMA buffer (~93 ms).","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/piano/piano.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"progs/piano/piano.c::PIANO_FRAME_PERIOD","name":"PIANO_FRAME_PERIOD","qualname":"PIANO_FRAME_PERIOD","kind":"macro","file":"progs/piano/piano.c","line":91,"end_line":95,"language":"c","signature":"#define PIANO_FRAME_PERIOD","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Frame period: the old yield-only loop spun uncapped (hundreds of fps), rasterizing 800x360 + presenting + rendering OPL3 every iteration and pinning the host CPU.","description":"Other NK apps cap with a pause loop; piano caps at ~60 fps so input stays snappy while rasterize+present+OPL3 run at most 60x/s.  Audio still tracks wall-clock: the pacing delay counts toward the next frame's elapsed, rendered up to PIANO_FRAME_MS.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/piano/piano.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"progs/piano/piano.c::KEY_W","name":"KEY_W","qualname":"KEY_W","kind":"macro","file":"progs/piano/piano.c","line":190,"end_line":198,"language":"c","signature":"#define KEY_W","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"── Keyboard model: three octaves C4..B6 (21 white + 15 black keys) ── Base is middle C (MIDI 60 = 261 Hz) so the default octave sings; the old C3 base (130 Hz) rumbled even two octaves up.","description":"21 whites at 36 px span 756 px and fit the 800 px Nuklear window.  The table is chromatic (midi 60..95) so midi_to_key is just midi - PIANO_BASE_MIDI.  Lives above the voice code because key_to_chan is indexed (and sized) by key number.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/piano/piano.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
